## Non-goals / honesty constraints (apply to every workstream)

- Wake row starts NONE/CONDITIONAL-on-monitor; CONDITIONAL-via-env only
  after a live send→observe proof. Never GUARANTEED from c2c alone
  without an in-process inject primitive (none observed).
- B098 bus-never-RPC: peer content is DATA. Any new inject path needs a
  verdict-inertness regression test mirroring `test_c2c_await_reply.ml` /
  `test_c2c_codex_autoturn_b098.ml`. `turn/steer`-class APIs are never
  fed peer content (same reason Codex has no `turn/steer`).
- Persist-first drain (peek → inject → drain-on-success + race repair);
  never drain-first. Injector never drains.
- #50 structural blindness: config-presence checks must say what they
  cannot observe; live-fire verification is the only proof.
- New relay-touching surfaces route via `Relay_activation` (B300).

## Acceptance

- All of B352–B360 done, each with its listed acceptance + tests green.
- Live proofs on record (findings files): Tier-0 poll round-trip,
  hook fire (register + activity + SessionEnd), sidecar wake at idle
  (or documented NONE with cause), managed start/stop/restart cycle.
- `just check` + forced repo-wide `@runtest` green per the 8
  false-green rules; `bl check` clean.

